  "notes": "R. Kelly's writing and production vehicle: a Chicago slow-jam duo, 1994–2000. The research gives \"54–89; ballads 54–67 half-time\" with five sourced tempos, four of which are in the ballad band, so 54–67 felt is the base with `halfTime` true. Three drum deltas are the entry's list: \"kick on 1 and the 8th before 3\" at one or two hits a bar, \"a hand-clap layer on 3\" stacked with the snare, and \"occasional 16th hat triplet fill\" — which is the one distinguishing hat parameter in this group of ballad models, encoded as a triplet roll vocabulary (`16T`/`32T`) at a real frequency over a hat lane that is otherwise at 0.1 fill density. Harmony is \"minor-7th/9th vamps of 2 or 4 bars, Rhodes and string pad\", so seventh and ninth carry 0.84 between them. \"Two-voice unison-and-third harmony (the duo sings mostly in parallel)\" is the very low leap share and the high chord-tone bias. The counter is the entry's \"signature high synth-bell countermelody\", carried at +12 with `bell_echo` leading — the research marks that claim `[LOW-CONF]` and it is repeated here. The bass is \"sustained synth bass on roots with a slide between chords; sub-forward mix\", so `glideProb` is high on a single-degree cell and there is no `bass808` block. \"No beat switches\" is why `switchUpProb` is near zero. ⚠ Confidence is **low** — the research rates the whole entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`, so the keys here are lane-level rather than named. ⚠ Every velocity, density and register number is INFERRED.",
